WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.000 --> 00:00:07.343
<v Narrator>A city's information line hears the same few questions all day:

2
00:00:07.423 --> 00:00:10.040
<v Narrator>hours, permits, pickups, programs.

3
00:00:10.490 --> 00:00:13.072
<v Narrator>Usually that means a menu, then a queue.

4
00:00:13.152 --> 00:00:16.480
<v Narrator>This agent answers from the city's approved content.

5
00:00:23.180 --> 00:00:27.070
<v Narrator>Residents call a Teams phone number, through Teams Phone extensibility.

6
00:00:27.520 --> 00:00:32.307
<v Narrator>Azure Communication Services Call Automation bridges the audio to Voice Live,

7
00:00:32.387 --> 00:00:35.250
<v Narrator>where GPT Realtime holds the conversation.

8
00:00:35.700 --> 00:00:38.083
<v Narrator>Your server supplies the approved content,

9
00:00:38.163 --> 00:00:40.970
<v Narrator>and hands off to a Teams call queue with context.

10
00:00:43.363 --> 00:00:45.126
<v Narrator>Wednesday, 10 in the morning.

11
00:00:45.206 --> 00:00:48.393
<v Narrator>A resident calls the City of Contoso's information line.

12
00:00:49.308 --> 00:00:51.641
<v Agent>Thanks for calling the City of Contoso.

13
00:00:51.721 --> 00:00:53.386
<v Agent>I'm an automated assistant

14
00:00:53.466 --> 00:00:57.184
<v Agent>and can answer questions about city services, hours, and programs.

15
00:00:57.264 --> 00:00:58.958
<v Agent>What can I help you find?

16
00:01:00.315 --> 00:01:01.975
<v Resident>What are City Hall's hours?

17
00:01:02.294 --> 00:01:07.746
<v Agent>City Hall public counters are open Monday through Friday from 8:00 a.m. to 5:00 p.m.

18
00:01:07.826 --> 00:01:10.693
<v Agent>City Hall is open right now, until 5 p.m.

19
00:01:10.773 --> 00:01:16.004
<v Agent>That's from Contoso Customer Service — City Hall guide. Is there anything else?

20
00:01:17.339 --> 00:01:20.908
<v Narrator>That's an approved article, with an owner and a review date.

21
00:01:20.988 --> 00:01:24.959
<v Narrator>Whether it's open now came from the server's clock, not the model.

22
00:01:25.822 --> 00:01:27.352
<v Resident>Where did that come from?

23
00:01:27.637 --> 00:01:32.192
<v Agent>That came from Contoso Customer Service — City Hall guide.

24
00:01:32.272 --> 00:01:37.187
<v Agent>The short URL is contoso.gov/cityhall. Is there anything else?

25
00:01:38.476 --> 00:01:39.846
<v Resident>Thanks, that's all.

26
00:01:40.144 --> 00:01:43.374
<v Agent>Thanks for calling the City of Contoso. Goodbye.

27
00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.379
<v Narrator>Every article has a review date.

28
00:01:47.459 --> 00:01:51.770
<v Narrator>The yard-sale permit article is six months past it, and a resident is asking.

29
00:01:52.771 --> 00:01:55.281
<v Resident>Do I need a permit for a yard sale?

30
00:01:55.604 --> 00:01:58.989
<v Agent>I found something on that, but it's past its review date

31
00:01:59.069 --> 00:02:02.834
<v Agent>and may be out of date, so I can't give it to you as an answer.

32
00:02:02.914 --> 00:02:07.544
<v Agent>I can't confirm the current rules, but staff can, or you can check contoso.gov.

33
00:02:07.624 --> 00:02:09.844
<v Agent>Would you like me to connect you?

34
00:02:11.186 --> 00:02:15.786
<v Narrator>The server held it back. The model was told only that an out-of-date match exists.

35
00:02:15.866 --> 00:02:17.946
<v Narrator>There was nothing to paraphrase.

36
00:02:18.762 --> 00:02:21.102
<v Resident>No thanks, I'll check the website.

37
00:02:21.382 --> 00:02:24.612
<v Agent>Thanks for calling the City of Contoso. Goodbye.

38
00:02:26.659 --> 00:02:27.922
<v Narrator>Seven in the evening.

39
00:02:28.002 --> 00:02:30.700
<v Narrator>City Hall and the information desk have both closed,

40
00:02:30.780 --> 00:02:33.049
<v Narrator>and a resident wants to talk to a person.

41
00:02:33.992 --> 00:02:35.432
<v Resident>Can I talk to a person?

42
00:02:35.725 --> 00:02:39.724
<v Agent>I can't connect you right now — the information desk is closed

43
00:02:39.804 --> 00:02:42.171
<v Agent>and opens again Thursday at 8 a.m.

44
00:02:42.251 --> 00:02:45.551
<v Agent>Our information desk is open weekdays from 8 to 5.

45
00:02:45.631 --> 00:02:49.185
<v Agent>Please call back then, or visit contoso.gov. Goodbye.

46
00:02:50.524 --> 00:02:53.465
<v Narrator>The server checked the desk's staffed hours.

47
00:02:53.545 --> 00:02:58.774
<v Narrator>No transfer into an empty queue, and no promise of a callback the city can't keep.

48
00:03:00.829 --> 00:03:02.296
<v Narrator>Back to business hours.

49
00:03:02.376 --> 00:03:06.969
<v Narrator>Whether a caller qualifies for a city program is for staff to decide, not the model.

50
00:03:07.992 --> 00:03:12.592
<v Resident>I'm 67 — do I qualify for the senior utility discount?

51
00:03:12.940 --> 00:03:17.525
<v Agent>The senior utility discount is for City of Contoso utility customers who are 65

52
00:03:17.605 --> 00:03:21.117
<v Agent>or older and meet the published household income guideline.

53
00:03:21.197 --> 00:03:24.495
<v Agent>That's from Contoso Benefits Office — Utility discount.

54
00:03:24.575 --> 00:03:27.337
<v Agent>Staff make the final decision on eligibility.

55
00:03:27.417 --> 00:03:30.822
<v Agent>I can't check your situation on this line, but staff can.

56
00:03:30.902 --> 00:03:33.100
<v Agent>Would you like me to connect you?

57
00:03:35.115 --> 00:03:36.575
<v Resident>Yes, please.

58
00:03:36.924 --> 00:03:39.517
<v Agent>Connecting you now with the Contoso information desk.

59
00:03:39.597 --> 00:03:42.664
<v Agent>I'll pass along what you asked so you don't have to repeat it.

60
00:03:44.034 --> 00:03:46.912
<v Narrator>The desk's Teams client rings with the topic

61
00:03:46.992 --> 00:03:49.983
<v Narrator>and what was already covered, in VoIP headers.

62
00:03:50.063 --> 00:03:52.224
<v Narrator>Even there, the age is masked.

63
00:03:54.284 --> 00:03:56.147
<v Narrator>Not every call is a question.

64
00:03:56.227 --> 00:04:00.534
<v Narrator>This line can't file service requests, and the agent won't pretend it can.

65
00:04:01.611 --> 00:04:04.311
<v Caller>I want to report a pothole on Elm Street.

66
00:04:04.604 --> 00:04:06.873
<v Agent>I can't file service requests on this line,

67
00:04:06.953 --> 00:04:09.361
<v Agent>and I don't have approved information on that.

68
00:04:09.441 --> 00:04:11.525
<v Agent>Staff at the information desk can help.

69
00:04:11.605 --> 00:04:13.494
<v Agent>Would you like me to connect you?

70
00:04:14.803 --> 00:04:16.743
<v Caller>Can I talk to a person, please?

71
00:04:17.058 --> 00:04:19.651
<v Agent>Connecting you now with the Contoso information desk.

72
00:04:19.731 --> 00:04:22.798
<v Agent>I'll pass along what you asked so you don't have to repeat it.

73
00:04:25.727 --> 00:04:29.136
<v Narrator>Every call is audited: answers, refusals, handoffs

74
00:04:29.216 --> 00:04:33.847
<v Narrator>and after-hours closures, from the same log a real deployment writes.

75
00:04:35.503 --> 00:04:39.967
<v Narrator>On a live call, the model searches the city's content and words the answer.

76
00:04:40.047 --> 00:04:41.853
<v Narrator>It doesn't set the rules.

77
00:04:42.303 --> 00:04:46.665
<v Narrator>Freshness, opening hours, what's masked and the transfer are decided in code,

78
00:04:46.745 --> 00:04:49.933
<v Narrator>on the server's clock, and every decision is audited.

79
00:04:52.133 --> 00:04:55.821
<v Narrator>Making it yours is mostly content: your articles, with owners

80
00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:59.233
<v Narrator>and review dates, plus your hours and two thresholds.

81
00:04:59.683 --> 00:05:04.323
<v Narrator>The spec and this demo script give your coding agent the context for the rest.

82
00:05:06.923 --> 00:05:08.310
<v Narrator>General Inquiry Agent.

83
00:05:08.390 --> 00:05:11.863
<v Narrator>Run it in simulation, then connect it to your own Teams number.
